IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra1-three-valued`
IMPORT `wra1-ch3-general`

-- wra1-sch5-6.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), Schedule 5 (universal credit and other working-age benefits) and
-- Schedule 6 (migration to universal credit), part wra1.
-- LAYER 1, the law objectively: it takes nobody's point of view.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- The raw text prints no paragraph numbers; they are counted by cross-heading (PLAN.md section 5), and the Act's own references
-- agree: Schedule 5 paragraph 4 cites "paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b)", and s 43(3)(m) cites "paragraphs 4, 5 and 6" of Schedule 6.
--   Schedule 5: 1 General, 2 Dual entitlement, 3 Movement between working-age benefits, 4 Hardship payments, 5 Earnings tapers.
--   Schedule 6: 1 General, 2 Claims before the appointed day, 3 Claims after the appointed day, 4 Awards,
--               5 Work-related requirements and sanctions, 6 Tax credits, 7 Supplementary.
-- Definitions are written over the core types (PLAN.md seam 9). The two definitions of "sanction" are not the same list, and
-- neither lists every provision of the core: each function says no only for what its own definition leaves out.
-- Reading an answer (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed and not ruled by a lawyer):
--   FALSE / JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (quoted in a FALSE-kind comment), or a supplied regulation says no
--   NOTHING            = not covered (the reason is in a NOTHING-kind comment)

§ `Schedule 5 paragraph 1 -- General`

-- (1) "In this Schedule 'relevant benefit' means (a) jobseeker's allowance, or (b) employment and support allowance."
-- src:3052 | (1) In this Schedule “relevant benefit“ means—
-- src:3053 | (a) jobseeker's allowance, or
-- src:3054 | (b) employment and support allowance.
@ref sch 5 para 1(1) (src:3052-3054)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1(1) the benefit is a relevant benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `contributory employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant benefit' means (a) jobseeker's allowance, or (b) employment and support allowance" (a closed definition)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (2) "In this Schedule 'work-related requirement' means (a) ... within the meaning of this Part, (b) ... within the meaning
-- of the Jobseekers Act 1995, or (c) ... within the meaning of Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007."
DECLARE `sch 5 para 1(2) regime a requirement belongs to` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 para 1(2)(a) this Part`
    `sch 5 para 1(2)(b) the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `sch 5 para 1(2)(c) Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
    `sch 5 para 1(2) some other regime`

-- src:3055 | (2) In this Schedule “work-related requirement“ means—
-- src:3056 | (a) a work-related requirement within the meaning of this Part,
-- src:3057 | (b) a work-related requirement within the meaning of the Jobseekers Act 1995, or
-- src:3058 | (c) a work-related requirement within the meaning of Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007.
@ref sch 5 para 1(2) (src:3055-3058)
GIVEN regime IS A `sch 5 para 1(2) regime a requirement belongs to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1(2) the requirement is a work-related requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER regime
    WHEN `sch 5 para 1(2)(a) this Part` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 1(2)(b) the Jobseekers Act 1995` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 1(2)(c) Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'work-related requirement' means" (a) to (c) (a closed definition)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (3) "In this Schedule 'sanction' means a reduction of benefit under (a) section 26 or 27, (b) section 6J or 6K of the
-- Jobseekers Act 1995, or (c) section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007."
-- src:3059 | (3) In this Schedule “sanction” means a reduction of benefit under—
-- src:3060 | (a) section 26 or 27,
-- src:3061 | (b) section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995, or
-- src:3062 | (c) section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007.
@ref sch 5 para 1(3) (src:3059-3062)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision that reduces an award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1(3) the reduction is a sanction` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `universal credit higher-level sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `universal credit other sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction after universal credit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `jobseeker's allowance other sanction after universal credit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `employment and support allowance sanction` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'sanction' means a reduction of benefit under" (a) to (c) (a closed definition); the interim-period provisions (JSA 19, 19A, 19B, WRA2007 11 to 13) and income support are not named here
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `Schedule 5 paragraphs 2 to 4 -- Dual entitlement, movement between benefits, hardship payments`

-- 2(1) "Regulations may make provision as to the amount payable by way of a relevant benefit where a person is entitled to that
-- benefit and universal credit." 2(2) "Regulations under sub-paragraph (1) may in particular provide for no amount to be payable
-- by way of a relevant benefit." The amount is what the regulations provide; the paragraph states none.
-- src:3064 | (1) Regulations may make provision as to the amount payable by way of a relevant benefit where a person is entitled to that benefit and universal credit.
-- src:3065 | (2) Regulations under sub-paragraph (1) may in particular provide for no amount to be payable by way of a relevant benefit.
@ref sch 5 para 2(1) (src:3064-3065)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to the relevant benefit and to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount regulations provide is payable by way of the relevant benefit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(1) the amount payable by way of the relevant benefit` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to the relevant benefit and to universal credit`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount is for regulations, which are not among the sources; a supplied amount (which may be nil, sub-paragraph (2)) is passed on as it is
    THEN `the amount regulations provide is payable by way of the relevant benefit`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "where a person is entitled to that benefit and universal credit"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 2(3) to (5) and 3(a) to (c): what regulations may provide for a person entitled to both, or who moves between them.
DECLARE `sch 5 para 2 and 3 provision regulations may make` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 para 2(3)(a) the application of work-related requirements`
    `sch 5 para 2(3)(b) the application of sanctions`
    `sch 5 para 2(4)(a) compliance with a requirement for a relevant benefit treated as compliance with a requirement for universal credit`
    `sch 5 para 2(4)(b) disapplying a requirement to impose, or to comply with, a work-related requirement`
    `sch 5 para 2(5)(a) the order in which sanctions are applied to awards of relevant benefit and universal credit`
    `sch 5 para 2(5)(b) securing that a sanction on a relevant benefit does not increase an award of universal credit`
    `sch 5 para 3(a) applying a universal credit sanction to the relevant benefit after a move from universal credit`
    `sch 5 para 3(b) applying a relevant benefit sanction to universal credit after a move to universal credit`
    `sch 5 para 3(c) applying a sanction on one relevant benefit to the other after a move between them`
    `sch 5 para 2 and 3 some other provision`

-- src:3066 | (3) Regulations may, where a person is entitled to a relevant benefit and universal credit—
-- src:3067 | (a) make provision as to the application of work-related requirements;
-- src:3068 | (b) make provision as to the application of sanctions.
-- src:3069 | (4) Provision under sub-paragraph (3)(a) includes in particular—
-- src:3070 | (a) provision securing that compliance with a work-related requirement for a relevant benefit is to be treated as compliance with a work-related requirement for universal credit;
-- src:3071 | (b) provision disapplying any requirement on the Secretary of State to impose, or a person to comply with, a work-related requirement for a relevant benefit or universal credit.
-- src:3072 | (5) Provision under sub-paragraph (3)(b) includes in particular—
-- src:3073 | (a) provision for the order in which sanctions are to be applied to awards of relevant benefit and universal credit;
-- src:3074 | (b) provision to secure that the application of a sanction to an award of a relevant benefit does not result in an increase of the amount of an award of universal credit.
-- src:3075 | Movement between working-age benefits
-- src:3076 | Regulations may provide—
-- src:3077 | (a) in a case where a person ceases to be entitled to universal credit and becomes entitled to a relevant benefit, for a sanction relating to the award of universal credit to be applied to the award of the relevant benefit;
-- src:3078 | (b) in a case where a person ceases to be entitled to a relevant benefit and becomes entitled to universal credit, for a sanction relating to the award of the relevant benefit to be applied to the award of universal credit;
-- src:3079 | (c) in a case where a person ceases to be entitled to one relevant benefit and becomes entitled to the other, for a sanction relating to the award of the former to apply to the award of the latter.
@ref sch 5 para 2(3) (src:3066-3079)
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 5 para 2 and 3 provision regulations may make`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 2 and 3 regulations may make this provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `sch 5 para 2(3)(a) the application of work-related requirements` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 2(3)(b) the application of sanctions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 2(4)(a) compliance with a requirement for a relevant benefit treated as compliance with a requirement for universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 2(4)(b) disapplying a requirement to impose, or to comply with, a work-related requirement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 2(5)(a) the order in which sanctions are applied to awards of relevant benefit and universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 2(5)(b) securing that a sanction on a relevant benefit does not increase an award of universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 3(a) applying a universal credit sanction to the relevant benefit after a move from universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 3(b) applying a relevant benefit sanction to universal credit after a move to universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 3(c) applying a sanction on one relevant benefit to the other after a move between them` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph 2(4) and (5) say "includes in particular", and nothing in these paragraphs says regulations may make no other provision
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 4 "Regulations under section 28 (hardship payments) may be made in relation to a person whose award of universal credit is
-- reduced by virtue of regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b) as in relation to a person whose award is reduced under
-- section 26 or 27."
-- src:3081 | Regulations under section 28 (hardship payments) may be made in relation to a person whose award of universal credit is reduced by virtue of regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b) as in relation to a person whose award is reduced under section 26 or 27.
@ref sch 5 para 4 (src:3081-3081)
GIVEN `the award of universal credit is reduced by virtue of regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4 regulations under section 28 may be made in relation to the person` MEANS
    IF `the award of universal credit is reduced by virtue of regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches a person "whose award of universal credit is reduced by virtue of regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b)"; a person reduced under section 26 or 27 is covered by section 28 itself
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 6 paragraph 1 -- General`

-- (2) "In this Schedule 'existing benefit' means (a) a benefit abolished under section 33(1); (b) any other prescribed benefit."
-- src:3095 | (2) In this Schedule “existing benefit“ means—
-- src:3096 | (a) a benefit abolished under section 33(1);
-- src:3097 | (b) any other prescribed benefit.
@ref sch 6 para 1(2) (src:3095-3097)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `regulations prescribe the benefit as an existing benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(2) the benefit is an existing benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 33(1) the benefit is abolished` benefit
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- the benefit is not named in s 33(1): it is an existing benefit only if prescribed, which regulations (not among the sources) decide
    OTHERWISE `regulations prescribe the benefit as an existing benefit`

-- (3) "In this Schedule 'appointed day' means the day appointed for the coming into force of section 1." Seam 10 of PLAN.md:
-- the day is s 150(3)'s, an input.
-- src:3098 | (3) In this Schedule “appointed day” means the day appointed for the coming into force of section 1.
@ref sch 6 para 1(3) (src:3098-3098)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `s 150(3) the day appointed for the coming into force of section 1` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(3) the day is the appointed day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 150(3) the day appointed for the coming into force of section 1`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'appointed day' means the day appointed for the coming into force of section 1": any other day is not the appointed day
    WHEN JUST appointed THEN JUST (day EQUALS appointed)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the day is appointed by order under s 150(3), which is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Schedule 6 paragraphs 2 to 7 -- what the regulations may include`

-- 1(1) "Regulations may make provision for the purposes of, or in connection with, replacing existing benefits with universal
-- credit." Paragraphs 2 to 4, 5, 6 and 7 each say "the provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes" a list.
DECLARE `sch 6 provision regulations may include` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 para 2(1)(a) a claim for universal credit made before the appointed day for a period beginning on or after that day`
    `sch 6 para 2(1)(b) a claim for universal credit made before the appointed day treated as a claim for an existing benefit`
    `sch 6 para 2(1)(c) a claim for an existing benefit made before the appointed day treated as a claim for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 2(2) an award on a claim made before the appointed day for a period before that day`
    `sch 6 para 3(1)(a) permanently or temporarily excluding a claim for universal credit after the appointed day by a person who has, or would be entitled to, an existing benefit`
    `sch 6 para 3(1)(b) temporarily excluding a claim for universal credit after the appointed day by any other person`
    `sch 6 para 3(1)(c) excluding entitlement to universal credit temporarily or for a particular period`
    `sch 6 para 3(1)(d) a claim for universal credit made after the appointed day treated as a claim for an existing benefit`
    `sch 6 para 3(1)(e) a claim for an existing benefit made after the appointed day treated as a claim for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 3(2) an award on a claim made after the appointed day for a period before that day`
    `sch 6 para 4(1)(a) terminating an award of an existing benefit`
    `sch 6 para 4(1)(b) making an award of universal credit, with or without application, to a person whose award of existing benefit is terminated`
    `sch 6 para 4(2)(a) requirements as to procedure, information or assessments for an award under para 4(1)(b)`
    `sch 6 para 4(2)(b) the consequences of failure to comply with such a requirement`
    `sch 6 para 4(2)(c)(i) disapplying or modifying conditions of entitlement to universal credit for the award`
    `sch 6 para 4(2)(c)(ii) disapplying or modifying any requirement to be assessed for capability for work or work-related activity`
    `sch 6 para 4(2)(d) the amount of such an award`
    `sch 6 para 4(2)(e) treating fulfilment of a condition for an existing benefit as fulfilment of an equivalent condition for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 4(3)(a) an award of universal credit not less than the terminated award, or not less by more than a prescribed amount`
    `sch 6 para 4(3)(b) disregarding a gap in entitlement of not more than a prescribed period`
    `sch 6 para 5(1)(a) the application of work-related requirements for relevant benefits`
    `sch 6 para 5(1)(b) the application of sanctions`
    `sch 6 para 5(2)(a) a claimant commitment for a relevant benefit treated as a claimant commitment for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 5(2)(b) a work-related requirement for a relevant benefit treated as one for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 5(2)(c) anything done relevant to compliance treated as done for compliance with a requirement for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 5(2)(d) temporarily disapplying provisions of this Part about work-related requirements`
    `sch 6 para 5(3)(a) a sanction relevant to a relevant benefit applied to an award of universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 5(3)(b) anything done relevant to a sanction treated as done for a sanction for universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 5(3)(c) temporarily disapplying provisions of this Part about the application of sanctions`
    `sch 6 para 6(a) modifying the application of the Tax Credits Act 2002`
    `sch 6 para 6(b) recovering overpayments of working tax credit or child tax credit, including treating them as overpayments of universal credit`
    `sch 6 para 7 disregarding a gap in entitlement to an existing benefit`
    `sch 6 some other provision`

-- src:3094 | (1) Regulations may make provision for the purposes of, or in connection with, replacing existing benefits with universal credit.
-- src:3095 | (2) In this Schedule “existing benefit“ means—
-- src:3096 | (a) a benefit abolished under section 33(1);
-- src:3097 | (b) any other prescribed benefit.
-- src:3098 | (3) In this Schedule “appointed day” means the day appointed for the coming into force of section 1.
-- src:3099 | Claims before the appointed day
-- src:3100 | (1) The provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes—
-- src:3101 | (a) provision for a claim for universal credit to be made before the appointed day for a period beginning on or after that day;
-- src:3102 | (b) provision for a claim for universal credit made before the appointed day to be treated to any extent as a claim for an existing benefit;
-- src:3103 | (c) provision for a claim for an existing benefit made before the appointed day to be treated to any extent as a claim for universal credit.
-- src:3104 | (2) The provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes provision, where a claim for universal credit is made (or is treated as made) before the appointed day, for an award on the claim to be made in respect of a period before the appointed day (including provision as to the conditions of entitlement for, and amount of, such an award).
-- src:3105 | Claims after the appointed day
-- src:3106 | (1) The provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes—
-- src:3107 | (a) provision permanently or temporarily excluding the making of a claim for universal credit after the appointed day by—
-- src:3108 | (i) a person to whom an existing benefit is awarded, or
-- src:3109 | (ii) a person who would be entitled to an existing benefit on making a claim for it;
-- src:3110 | (b) provision temporarily excluding the making of a claim for universal credit after the appointed day by any other person;
-- src:3111 | (c) provision excluding entitlement to universal credit temporarily or for a particular period;
-- src:3112 | (d) provision for a claim for universal credit made after the appointed day to be treated to any extent as a claim for an existing benefit;
-- src:3113 | (e) provision for a claim for an existing benefit made after the appointed day to be treated to any extent as a claim for universal credit.
-- src:3114 | (2) The provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes provision, where a claim for universal credit is made (or is treated as made) after the appointed day, for an award on the claim to be made in respect of a period before the appointed day (including provision as to the conditions of entitlement for, and amount of, such an award).
-- src:3115 | Awards
-- src:3116 | (1) The provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes—
-- src:3117 | (a) provision for terminating an award of an existing benefit;
-- src:3118 | (b) provision for making an award of universal credit, with or without application, to a person whose award of existing benefit is terminated.
-- src:3119 | (2) The provision referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(b) includes—
-- src:3120 | (a) provision imposing requirements as to the procedure to be followed, information to be supplied or assessments to be undergone in relation to an award by virtue of that sub-paragraph or an application for such an award;
-- src:3121 | (b) provision as to the consequences of failure to comply with any such requirement;
-- src:3122 | (c) provision as to the terms on which, and conditions subject to which, such an award is made, including—
-- src:3123 | (i) provision temporarily or permanently disapplying, or otherwise modifying, conditions of entitlement to universal credit in relation to the award;
-- src:3124 | (ii) provision temporarily or permanently disapplying, or otherwise modifying, any requirement under this Part for a person to be assessed in respect of capability for work or work-related activity;
-- src:3125 | (d) provision as to the amount of such an award;
-- src:3126 | (e) provision that fulfilment of any condition relevant to entitlement to an award of an existing benefit, or relevant to the amount of such an award, is to be treated as fulfilment of an equivalent condition in relation to universal credit.
-- src:3127 | (3) Provision under sub-paragraph (2)(d) may secure that where an award of universal credit is made by virtue of sub-paragraph (1)(b)—
-- src:3128 | (a) the amount of the award is not less than the amount to which the person would have been entitled under the terminated award, or is not less than that amount by more than a prescribed amount;
-- src:3129 | (b) if the person to whom it is made ceases to be entitled to universal credit for not more than a prescribed period, the gap in entitlement is disregarded in calculating the amount of any new award of universal credit.
-- src:3130 | Work-related requirements and sanctions
-- src:3131 | (1) The provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes—
-- src:3132 | (a) provision relating to the application of work-related requirements for relevant benefits;
-- src:3133 | (b) provision relating to the application of sanctions.
-- src:3134 | (2) The provision referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(a) includes—
-- src:3135 | (a) provision that a claimant commitment for a relevant benefit is to be treated as a claimant commitment for universal credit;
-- src:3136 | (b) provision that a work-related requirement for a relevant benefit is treated as a work-related requirement for universal credit;
-- src:3137 | (c) provision for anything done which is relevant to compliance with a work-related requirement for a relevant benefit to be treated as done for the purposes of compliance with a work-related requirement for universal credit;
-- src:3138 | (d) provision temporarily disapplying any provision of this Part in relation to work-related requirements for universal credit.
-- src:3139 | (3) The provision referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(b) includes—
-- src:3140 | (a) provision for a sanction relevant to an award of a relevant benefit to be applied to an award of universal credit;
-- src:3141 | (b) provision for anything done which is relevant to the application of a sanction for a relevant benefit to be treated as done for the purposes of the application of a sanction for universal credit;
-- src:3142 | (c) provision temporarily disapplying any provision of this Part in relation to the application of sanctions.
-- src:3143 | (4) In this paragraph—
-- src:3144 | “relevant benefit” means—
-- src:3145 | jobseeker's allowance,
-- src:3146 | employment and support allowance, and
-- src:3147 | income support;
-- src:3148 | “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:3149 | for universal credit, a work-related requirement within the meaning of this Part;
-- src:3150 | for jobseeker's allowance, a requirement imposed—
-- src:3151 | by virtue of regulations under section 8 or 17A of the Jobseekers Act 1995,
-- src:3152 | by a jobseeker's direction (within the meaning of section 19A of that Act),
-- src:3153 | by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:3154 | by a direction under section 2F of that Act;
-- src:3155 | for employment and support allowance, a requirement imposed—
-- src:3156 | by virtue of regulations under section 8, 9, 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007,
-- src:3157 | by a direction under section 15 of that Act,
-- src:3158 | by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:3159 | by a direction under section 2F of that Act;
-- src:3160 | for income support, a requirement imposed—
-- src:3161 | by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:3162 | by a direction under section 2F of that Act;
-- src:3163 | “sanction” means a reduction of benefit under—
-- src:3164 | section 26 or 27 above,
-- src:3165 | section 19, 19A or 19B of the Jobseekers Act 1995,
-- src:3166 | section 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, or
-- src:3167 | section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992.
-- src:3168 | Tax credits
-- src:3169 | In relation to the replacement of working tax credit and child tax credit with universal credit, the provision referred to in paragraph 1(1) includes—
-- src:3170 | (a) provision modifying the application of the Tax Credits Act 2002 (or of any provision made under it);
-- src:3171 | (b) provision for the purposes of recovery of overpayments of working tax credit or child tax credit (including in particular provision for treating overpayments of working tax credit or child tax credit as if they were overpayments of universal credit).
-- src:3172 | Supplementary
-- src:3173 | Regulations under paragraph 1(1) may secure the result that any gap in entitlement to an existing benefit (or what would, but for the provisions of this Part, be a gap in entitlement to an existing benefit) is to be disregarded for the purposes of provision under such regulations.
@ref sch 6 para 1(1) (src:3094-3173)
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 6 provision regulations may include`
      `it is for the purposes of, or in connection with, replacing existing benefits with universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(1) regulations may include this provision` MEANS
    IF `it is for the purposes of, or in connection with, replacing existing benefits with universal credit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER provision
        WHEN `sch 6 some other provision` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "includes" does not close the list of provision regulations may make
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for provision "for the purposes of, or in connection with, replacing existing benefits with universal credit"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 6 paragraph 5(4) -- relevant benefit, work-related requirement, sanction`

-- (4) "'relevant benefit' means jobseeker's allowance, employment and support allowance, and income support"
-- src:3144 | “relevant benefit” means—
-- src:3145 | jobseeker's allowance,
-- src:3146 | employment and support allowance, and
-- src:3147 | income support;
@ref sch 6 para 5(4) (src:3144-3147)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 5(4) the benefit is a relevant benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `contributory employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income support` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant benefit' means" jobseeker's allowance, employment and support allowance, and income support (a closed definition)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (4) "'work-related requirement' means for universal credit, a work-related requirement within the meaning of this Part; for
-- jobseeker's allowance, a requirement imposed by virtue of regulations under section 8 or 17A of the Jobseekers Act 1995, by a
-- jobseeker's direction, by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- by a direction under section 2F of that Act; for employment and support allowance ...; for income support ..."
DECLARE `sch 6 para 5(4) source of a requirement` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 para 5(4) universal credit: a work-related requirement within the meaning of this Part`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: regulations under section 8 or 17A of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: a jobseeker's direction within the meaning of section 19A of that Act`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: a direction under section 2F of that Act`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: regulations under section 8, 9, 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: a direction under section 15 of that Act`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: a direction under section 2F of that Act`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) income support: regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) income support: a direction under section 2F of that Act`
    `sch 6 para 5(4) some other source`

-- src:3148 | “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:3149 | for universal credit, a work-related requirement within the meaning of this Part;
-- src:3150 | for jobseeker's allowance, a requirement imposed—
-- src:3151 | by virtue of regulations under section 8 or 17A of the Jobseekers Act 1995,
-- src:3152 | by a jobseeker's direction (within the meaning of section 19A of that Act),
-- src:3153 | by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:3154 | by a direction under section 2F of that Act;
-- src:3155 | for employment and support allowance, a requirement imposed—
-- src:3156 | by virtue of regulations under section 8, 9, 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007,
-- src:3157 | by a direction under section 15 of that Act,
-- src:3158 | by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:3159 | by a direction under section 2F of that Act;
-- src:3160 | for income support, a requirement imposed—
-- src:3161 | by virtue of regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:3162 | by a direction under section 2F of that Act;
@ref sch 6 para 5(4) (src:3148-3162)
GIVEN source IS A `sch 6 para 5(4) source of a requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 5(4) the requirement is a work-related requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) universal credit: a work-related requirement within the meaning of this Part` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: regulations under section 8 or 17A of the Jobseekers Act 1995` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: a jobseeker's direction within the meaning of section 19A of that Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) JSA: a direction under section 2F of that Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: regulations under section 8, 9, 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: a direction under section 15 of that Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) ESA: a direction under section 2F of that Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) income support: regulations under section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 5(4) income support: a direction under section 2F of that Act` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'work-related requirement' means" the listed sources (a closed definition)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (4) "'sanction' means a reduction of benefit under section 26 or 27 above, section 19, 19A or 19B of the Jobseekers Act 1995,
-- section 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, or section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992."
-- src:3163 | “sanction” means a reduction of benefit under—
-- src:3164 | section 26 or 27 above,
-- src:3165 | section 19, 19A or 19B of the Jobseekers Act 1995,
-- src:3166 | section 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, or
-- src:3167 | section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992.
@ref sch 6 para 5(4) (src:3163-3167)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision that reduces an award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 5(4) the reduction is a sanction` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `universal credit higher-level sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `universal credit other sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `jobseeker's allowance other sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `jobseeker's allowance ceasing to be available` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `employment and support allowance interim sanction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income support sanction` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'sanction' means a reduction of benefit under" the listed sections (a closed definition); the sanctions inserted for the time after universal credit (JSA 6J and 6K, WRA2007 11J) are not among them
    OTHERWISE FALSE
